  "description": "GPU cloth solver for MonoGame: a compute shader integrates the particles, relaxes the constraints and computes the normals, and the positions never leave the GPU. Verlet integration with Jacobi relaxation, plastic bending so creases stay, long-range attachments, colliders with friction, self-collision through a spatial hash, cuts, rips and tearing under strain, and drag against wind you set every frame. Solver only - you fetch the particles in your own vertex shader and draw the sheet yourself. Requires Windows and the compute-capable MonoGame fork. The solver ships as HLSL and is compiled by your content pipeline.",
